Add a generic software PWM driver as a fallback when no dedicated hardware PWM pins are available.
This implementation leverages a single hardware timer interrupt as a time base to derive an arbitrary number of software-controlled PWM channels. The period is the same for all channels.
    
This enables use of LED brightness and blink APIs. Tested on Nucleo H563ZI with this overlay:
    
```
/ {
    status_leds: status_leds {
        compatible = "pwm-leds";
        status_led_1: status_led_1 {
            pwms = <&soft_pwm 0 PWM_MSEC(10) PWM_POLARITY_NORMAL>;
            label = "1";
        };
    };

    soft_pwm: soft_pwm {
        compatible = "zephyr,pwm-bitbang";
        #pwm-cells = <3>;
        timer = <&tim6_counter>;
        pwm-gpios = <&gpiob 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; 
    };
};
    
&timers6 {
    status = "okay";
    st,prescaler = <24999>;
    tim6_counter: counter {
        status = "okay";
    };
};
```

